<title>USA: TABLE- Royal Appliance Q2 shr $0.04 vs $0.05.</title>
<headline>TABLE- Royal Appliance Q2 shr $0.04 vs $0.05.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>COMPARATIVE FINANCIAL RESULTS</p>
<p>							1997	    1996</p>
<p>3 months to June 30</p>
<p> Net sales				  $61,070,000   $62,969,000</p>
<p> Gross margin				17,739,000    16,504,000</p>
<p> Net income				     919,000     1,328,000</p>
<p> Per share					   0.04	    0.05</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>   common shares			   24,193,000    24,296,000</p>
<p>6 months to June 30</p>
<p> Net sales				  119,688,000   115,231,000</p>
<p> Gross margin				33,973,000    30,267,000</p>
<p> Net income				   1,525,000     1,660,000</p>
<p> Per share					   0.06	    0.07</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>   common shares			   24,289,000    24,142,000</p>
<p>Note: The company said the second quarter of 1996 included a one-time gain of $0.02 per share from the sale of a building.</p>
<p>The company also said it expects the initial retail pipeline shipments of the new Dirt Devil Mop Vac will help sales in the third quarter.</p>
<p>Royal Appliance Manufacturing Co.</p>
</text>
